# The Vercel project builds from web/, but the CLI uploads from the repo root
# (that is where the project link lives, because the project's Root Directory
# setting is "web"). Without this, every sibling project comes along for the
# ride -- Rust target dirs, Hardhat artifacts, subgraph build output, several
# node_modules trees -- and the upload trips Vercel's 15,000 file limit.
#
# Nothing here is used by the Next.js build.

liquid-pass-master/
contracts/
subscription/
subgraph/
oracle/
bench/
extension/
docs/

# Build output and caches anywhere in the tree
**/node_modules/
**/target/
**/.next/
**/artifacts/
**/cache/
**/test-results/
**/playwright-report/

# Never upload a key, whatever else changes
**/*.key
